---
===== path query
Query the local cache: load every step into one JSON array and transform it with a jaq (jq) filter

Usage: path query [OPTIONS] <FILTER>

Arguments:
  <FILTER>
          jaq (jq) filter to run over the scoped step array (use `.` to emit the array unchanged)

Options:
      --source <SOURCE>
          Select cached files by source prefix (claude/gemini/codex/opencode/cursor/pi/git/github)

      --id <IDS>
          Load a specific cached document by id (repeatable)

      --input <INPUT>
          Load an off-cache document (`-` for stdin; repeatable)

      --project <PROJECT>
          Keep only paths whose base resolves to this project directory

      --project-under <PROJECT_UNDER>
          Keep only sessions whose project directory (the path base) lies under this directory (subtree match; the session's recorded working directory, not the files it touched), and scope the implicit sync to it likewise

      --kind <KIND>
          Keep only paths whose meta.kind matches this selector (semver prefix, e.g. `agent-coding-session` or `…/v1.0`)

  -c, --compact
          Force compact (single-line) JSON output

  -r, --raw
          Output raw strings without JSON quotes/escaping (like `jq -r`). Applies only to string results; non-strings still print as JSON. Handy for piping a column of ids/paths into another command, or reading text/diff content. Composes with `-c`

      --no-sync
          Skip the automatic cache sync that runs before the query

      --pretty
          Pretty-print JSON output

      --picker <PICKER>
          Backend for the interactive fuzzy picker used by `share`, `resume`, and `p import <provider>`. `auto` (default) uses the embedded skim picker and falls back to external `fzf` only when skim isn't compiled in; a hint is printed if `fzf` is also on PATH. `fzf`/`skim` force one backend and error if it isn't available

          Possible values:
          - auto: Pick whichever backend is available; prefer the embedded skim picker and fall back to external `fzf` when skim isn't compiled in. When external `fzf` is also on `PATH`, a one-time hint is printed to stderr advising `--picker fzf` for users who want their fzf config / keybindings
          - fzf:  Force the external `fzf` binary. Errors if it isn't on `PATH`
          - skim: Force the embedded skim picker. Errors if path-cli was built with `--no-default-features`
          
          [default: auto]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Each array element wraps a Toolpath step:

  {
    "cache_id": "claude-abc123",
    "path": { "id": …, "base": …, "meta": { "kind": …, "source": … } },
    "step":   { "id": …, "parents": [...], "actor": …, "timestamp": … },
    "change": { "<artifact>": { "raw": …, "structural": … } },
    "meta":   { … },
    "dead_end": false
  }

The fields under `change[].structural` are defined by the path's kind;
run `path kind <kind>` for the schema, or `path query --kind … '.[0]'` to
read a sample. Identity is the triple (cache_id, path.id, step.id).

A real cache mixes provider and tool versions, so a field's shape can vary
(e.g. `tool_uses[]` is sometimes an object, sometimes a bare name string).
Guard element access with `?` (`.name?`) and `// empty` so one odd value
doesn't abort the run; sample with `'.[0]'` when unsure.

Examples:
  path query 'map(select(any(.. | strings; test("RefCell"))))'
  path query 'map(select(any(.change | keys[]; endswith("cmd_resume.rs"))))'
  path query --source claude 'map(select(any(.change[].structural.tool_uses[]?; .name? == "Bash" and .result.is_error? == true)))'
  path query 'group_by(.path.meta.source) | map({source: .[0].path.meta.source, steps: length})'
  path query -r '.[].cache_id' | sort -u            # raw ids, pipeable to xargs/grep
  path query -r '.[0].change[].structural.text'     # read a turn's text, unescaped
